WEBVTT

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.690
The interstellar, multi-generational colony ship,

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.770
which once carried the people of Serenity,

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.250
now wanders the galaxy as the golden ghost ship.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.420
The Bentenmaru, led by Kato Marika,

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.910
finds itself inside this ship,
along with the Serenity royal family's

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.990
seventh princess, Gruier Serenity.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.740
The ghost ship is jumping.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.500
All crew, brace for impact!

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.950
The ghost ship disappears into subspace once more.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.960
Will its mysteries finally be revealed?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.670
Are you okay in your spacesuit?

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.330
Y-Yes.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.460
Let me know if you have
trouble breathing or anything.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.000
I'm fine.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.550
This is up.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.890
And then, the opposite direction is down.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:49.270
In zero gravity, you won't know
which way you're facing.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.730
So it helps to remember which way is which.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.820
Then, the way my head is pointing is up.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.200
And you're in front of me, right?

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.450
That's right.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.230
The spinning's stopped, so the whole ghost ship is zero-g.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:05.870
Are you okay to go?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.870
I have to go.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.630
Come, Princess.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.340
Let's board the legendary ghost ship.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.640
Don't put out your hand.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.100
I'll rely on you if you do.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.890
What you can't do for yourself,
you can rely on others for.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.270
You're alone in space.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.150
Everyone's alone.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.820
No one will offer a hand to someone
who doesn't try to help herself.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.490
I'm going to jump.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.000
They're just like a prince and a princess.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.550
Can we open it?

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:08.010
It isn't a complicated lock. Don't worry.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.480
Can we connect to the ghost ship?

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.730
Coorie's on the bridge working on it.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.480
It's surprising the first time you see it.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.150
You may know intellectually that
cyborgs don't need spacesuits, but...

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.700
The power cable from the Bentenmaru is connected.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:29.370
Hyakume,

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.040
turn it on.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:31.870
Gotcha.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.290
Starting with a standard 200.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.790
What do we do?

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.290
Up the power a bit?

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.670
No, this is fine.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:47.800
On the other side of the hatch,
you'll have 0.8 atmospheres, 24% oxygen.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:51.100
No poisonous gases or radiation detected so far.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.820
Bridge to Captain Marika!

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:02.940
Can you hear me?

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.240
We're about to go inside the ghost ship.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.320
Find anything?

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.030
Yeah, several things.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:11.160
The ghost ship has two landing decks.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.540
And there are signs of a ship infiltrating
from another, separate deck.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:20.040
Given the ship's layout,
it's hard to imagine that battleship simply docked.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:24.670
But I don't know how many people they brought with them.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:28.680
It'd be nice if we could connect
to the ghost ship's host computer.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.100
Thanks.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.760
Keep it up.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.140
Roger.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:33.930
You heard that.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:34.980
Right, Gruier?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.190
Let's hurry.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.320
The air's all right.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.030
You can remove your helmets.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.420
Okay, Gruier. Where should we go?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:01.250
We aren't heading for the
engine or the bridge first?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.380
We'll let the Serenity folks handle that.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.260
They've sent plenty of search teams,
so they must know about those places.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.390
How irresponsible...

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.510
Well, we are pirates.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.060
We should hurry to the treasure.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.230
Understood.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.200
It isn't working.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.410
Do we need another safe-cracker?

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.580
I think it's fine.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.490
Leave it to me.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.420
We're near the engine and power couplings,

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.670
as well as the buffer tanks for maintaining
the ship's atmospheric pressure,

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:51.970
and the circulation system for
the ship's disinfectants.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.350
The sleepers...

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.350
Aren't the cold sleep units at the ship's center?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:01.900
See?

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.690
Told you we could leave it to them.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:04.480
Yeah...

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:12.620
If the lights are on, you can assume the
monitoring system is powered on as well.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:15.950
So they know where we are, huh?

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.500
Nothing we can do about that.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.750
Take a right.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.190
If there were anything...

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:55.290
If there were anything in the
universe with real universal value,

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.450
what do you think it would be?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.080
Universal value?

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.750
Something truly irreplaceable.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.500
Precious metals are valuable,

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.790
but with enough time and effort,
you can make as much as you like.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.090
Art or culture?

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.550
That's true.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.550
Even in the distant future,

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:19.850
as long as civilization is still civilized,
art and history will retain their value.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.480
Civilization, huh?

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:27.570
What's this?

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.940
It's pretty old.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.490
This is amazing!

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.450
What is it?

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:37.950
Some weird monitor?

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.450
A mechanical display.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:44.170
Each pixel contains tiny gears
and miniature crank shafts.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.750
It displays text by rapidly switching among

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.920
the three primary colors, and black and white.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.800
Never seen a working one before.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.180
Go on.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.890
It needs the name of a royal family member.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.970
You can enter the name one letter at a time.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:08.710
Beyond this door is a temperature-controlled, low-gravity environment.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:09.730
Correct?

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.820
Should be.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:14.900
It's pressurized, but most of the
atmosphere is nitrogen gas.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.280
With a minor amount of inert gases.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.330
Perfect for long-term preservation.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.580
So we finally get to see our treasure?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:27.500
I think what you're all expecting
isn't to be found aboard this ship.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.250
But there's treasure, right?

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.170
I'll open the door.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:44.520
Kind of empty for a treasure chest.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.770
This isn't the right place?

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:48.650
I think the other storerooms will be similar.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.610
What about the art? The paintings?

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.190
Didn't they wish to preserve this stuff
so badly that they used nitrogen?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:10:00.740
It's true that the Serenity royal family kept
pre-FTL cultural artifacts on the golden ghost ship.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:06.870
But nearly all were taken out and sold
during various past economic crises.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.210
So that's what those search teams were for.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:09.890
Yes.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:14.920
You've already learned how to do it?

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.630
I watched Hyakume.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:20.390
Wow... I guess it's the royal blood.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.530
The sleeper area.

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:51.580
Yact Shatro Heim Aries?

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.340
It's a mountain goat.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.340
It's the ancestor of the sheep kept on Serenity.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:00.300
So there are even sleeping sheep, huh?

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:09.230
Then this is the place the ghost ship
was originally designed for, isn't it?

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:15.020
It holds the genes and live samples
for every living thing in the Serenity system.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.530
A gene bank?

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.860
That's amazing, Gruier.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.780
The Serenity royal family is amazing.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.780
They think on a big scale.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.030
There aren't any people here.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:33.710
Everything here is a mere backup
of a life form carried by the colony ship.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:39.010
Even were we able to duplicate Serenity's
natural environment on another planet,

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.630
that's all it would ever be.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:43.140
Then there's something more important, right?

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:12.540
What is it?

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:16.540
A long time ago, it would have
asked for a drop of blood.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.780
Leave this to me.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.130
What is this?

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:43.880
Were you planning to shut the hatch
once you were through?

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:49.930
I gave up on that idea when
you opened the big hatch.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:55.640
Is this the important thing
you were talking about?

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:56.690
Yes.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.560
Oh, my. How old is this?

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:03.070
I've never seen a plant this size.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.150
Do you know what it is?

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:06.240
May I tell them?

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:06.950
Yes.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.530
It's an artificial womb.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:16.160
The part that looks like a bud with all the cords
is an artificial womb where fertilized eggs grow,

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.540
and the equipment to maintain it.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:22.540
The central block is a system for
coating and tuning the genes.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.880
Am I right?

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:27.420
You could tell all that just by looking at it?

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:29.760
Doctors are terrifying.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.010
I made up half of that.

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:34.100
I just thought I'd see what you'd say.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.020
I figured it was something like that.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:41.310
This is where the royal family was born.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:44.820
I'm reading another signal.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:46.400
Get ready.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.280
Understood.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.910
Yes, this is Marika.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.580
This is the Bentenmaru.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:58.410
Good, I was worried we wouldn't be
able to communicate within the ship.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.170
Appears to be fine.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.960
Do you have our location?

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.550
I finally made it into the ship's network.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.590
I can see your general position.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:11.260
As well as three or four other signals moving around.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:14.180
One of them is heading toward your location.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.390
Thanks.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:20.940
Looks like they're here.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.790
No one move!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.460
It seems I made it in time.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.000
I'm relieved to see you haven't done anything yet.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:46.420
No, everything is over.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:50.010
When the people of Serenity ceased to need the royal family,

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:53.010
our role ended!

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:55.850
What good would retrieving this thing do?

00:15:55.850 --> 00:16:00.600
But destroying it will also accomplish nothing, correct?

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:03.310
The first king was born from this rose spring,

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:06.230
and he founded the royal family.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.440
You must know that, Gruier.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.860
Even if that history is false,

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.700
Serenity's prosperity and stability are real!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.950
Our bloodline isn't the issue.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:20.080
The royal family's role is over.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.160
Even if we use the rose spring,

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.040
it won't bring back the glory of the past
or the royal family's prestige!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.790
That's where you're wrong!

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.010
You're not seeing the reality—

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.300
Gruier, down.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.720
Marika?

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:40.560
Yotof! Catherine!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:41.890
I'm right here.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:43.600
Forgive me.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.750
She's awake!

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.880
Sorry to do this when you've just woken up,

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.420
but I need your authorization.

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:13.380
Got it!

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:17.760
Here.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.440
What are you both doing here?

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.650
Our interests were aligned,
I guess you could say.

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:36.200
Why did you act in such
an unprincipled manner?

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.400
What do you mean?

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:40.370
Forcing me to breathe that weird gas...

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.660
What did you mean to achieve?

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.540
A peaceful resolution.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:49.330
The Serenity troops couldn't open fire
on their princess, could they?

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:53.090
Only an unprincipled pirate could do that.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:05.350
So, what will you do now?

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:07.640
Return the ghost ship to its home.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:12.690
The ghost ship is heading for the Serenity system?

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:14.150
That's right.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:18.570
Making quantum probability theory
and multi-D universe theory work

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.910
within the same space-time
string was very difficult.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.540
What?!

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:27.620
Why do you think I came to the
ghost ship in the first place?

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.630
You never told us.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.510
Don't worry.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.310
The bio-plant is already finished.

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:47.180
What do you mean?

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.400
The rose spring has dried up.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:54.980
It was drained dry of genetic samples and bio-cells.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:56.940
I can't be...

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.500
I take that back.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.790
It had one left, but then it was finished.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.750
One left?

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:15.500
The last member of the Serenity
royal family to be born from this space ship.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:19.050
The baby was slightly premature, but it's okay.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:22.010
Say hello to your big sister.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:35.730
I almost...

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:40.030
killed this child?

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:45.280
You came just in time to save it,
so everything worked out.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:52.170
Any later and it would've stayed frozen,
unable to be revived.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:55.500
Everything works out when you're a pirate!

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:56.290
Right?

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:03.300
Thank you.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:17.440
But how did you and Yotof exchange signals?

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:21.070
Can you read minds?

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.070
Nope.

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:28.120
Before we made contact with the ghost ship,
I kicked you off the bridge, right?

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:32.040
I sent a code to the Serendipity then.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.830
Fortunately, Yotof's pretty smart.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.790
You did it that long ago?

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:41.210
Then Hilde and I were being
deceived the entire time.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:43.840
We didn't really deceive you.
We just didn't tell you.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:59.400
You really are like your father...

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:01.360
Like Captain Kato.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:02.800
Am I?

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:03.530
How?

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:05.910
Your deviousness.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:06.530
In a good way.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.030
Aw, jeez.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.790
We're returning to normal space.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:22.140
This is Gruier Serenity and Grunhilde Serenity,
legitimate heirs to the Serenity throne.

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:26.760
True darkness feels so empty.

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.550
We have returned with the golden ghost ship.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:33.270
I can't even see my own palm.

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.800
This colony ship once brought glory to the royal family.

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:37.980
The stars above are the only light.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:42.100
After a thousand years, the golden
ghost ship has returned to Serenity.

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:47.270
My senses sharpen again, like a wild animal's.

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:49.600
Citizens, hear my words.

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:50.580
My conscience heads inward, inward

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.330
Good luck, Gruier.

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:52.460
My conscience heads inward, inward

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:53.660
on an arduous, testing journey.

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:55.540
Bentenmaru, full speed ahead!

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:55.980
Set a course for Sea of the Morningstar!

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:57.960
The fragile blade I believed in

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:58.790
Roger!

00:21:58.790 --> 00:21:59.620
The fragile blade I believed in

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:03.380
lost its shine.

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:08.300
Into the holy space I throw myself.

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:11.260
A Return from Eternity

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:11.340
Into the holy space I throw myself.

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:18.480
Find the answer no matter how hard, Black Holy.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:25.220
Although I'm bad at calculating while moving forward,

00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:34.970
I knew that it was alright to do things naturally.

00:22:35.860 --> 00:22:42.250
Hey, try to open your eyes once again,

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:49.260
even if it's just somewhere you went to see the stars.

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:56.190
The energy in your heart cannot be extinguished.

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:01.660
Awake to a differently colored dawn.

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:11.940
Into the holy space I throw myself.

00:23:11.940 --> 00:23:18.780
Find the answer no matter how hard, Black Holy.

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:25.510
Even if the horizons of the distant space are gone,

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:30.700
I feel no fear.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:34.300
I feel free.

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:42.310
The storm gives way to a new peace,

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:45.520
and the princess begins life as a normal girl.

00:23:46.490 --> 00:23:48.070
As time begins to move,

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:52.110
Kato Marika sets out on a plan for a friend.

00:23:53.870 --> 00:23:55.660
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:57.290
Marika sends an invitation.

00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:59.000
Look forward to it.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:05.000
Marika Sends an Invitation

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.490
Everything works out
when you're a pirate!
